This reads `mangled_cur[1]`. If `mangled_cur` points to the last character of the buffer (at index `Size-1`), then `mangled_cur[1]` reads `Buffer[Size]` which is the null terminator - that's fine. But if `mangled_cur` points to `Buffer[Size]` (the null terminator itself), then `mangled_cur[1]` reads `Buffer[Size+1]` which is **past the end of the buffer**!

So the bug is: when `mangled_cur` points to the null terminator at `Buffer[Size]`, `ParseTwoCharToken` reads `mangled_cur[1]` which is out of bounds.

